OL,3,GNEWSAThe '50s Slough estate that felt
OL,4,Alike 'paradise'
OL,5,
OL,6,F"All we had was a small amount of
OL,7,Ffurniture in the van and a budgie in a
OL,8,Fcage."
OL,10,FDenis Collman remembers clearly the day
OL,11,Fin 1956 when he and his mum, dad and
OL,12,Fthree brothers squeezed into the back
OL,13,Fof a removal van, leaving behind their
OL,14,Fcramped two-room flat in London's
OL,15,FLadbroke Grove for a new life in
OL,16,FSlough.
OL,18,FWhen the vehicle pulled up to to the
OL,19,Fthen fledgling Britwell Estate he said:
OL,20,F"It was absolute heaven moving into a
OL,21,Fbrand new house with a bath, a flushing
OL,22,Ftoilet and bed all of my own."
OL,23,APub: 29-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
